{"id":"fact-example-001","type":"code_quirk","fact":"Example: The UserService caches results for 5 minutes, so updates may not appear immediately in queries.","recommendation":"Use cache invalidation after writes, or query with { fresh: true } option.","confidence":"medium","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"discovered during debugging","date":"2026-01-15"}],"tags":["caching","user-service"],"affectedFiles":["src/lib/services/user.service.ts"],"affectedServices":["UserService"],"createdAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "fact-frontend-harness-lifecycle-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "Frontend AI-Harness/tmux sessions are spawned in createTab (Frontend/API.hs), not by the dispatcher tab factory: createHarnessTab calls the injected _fe_startHarness seam, persists the returned TmuxConfig into _sm_kind, and registers the handle in the shared _fe_harnesses map (== _env_harnesses, the same harnessRef IORef wired in CLI/Commands.hs). handleSend then routes SkHarness sessions to _hh_send/_hh_receive instead of the LLM provider.", "recommendation": "To add/modify frontend harness behaviour, edit createHarnessTab + handleSend in Frontend/API.hs and the _fe_startHarness impl in CLI/Commands.hs (delegates to startHarnessByName). The dispatcher's Tab.Harness.mkTabHarness only ADOPTS an already-running harness.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a / PR fix-frontend-harness-tmux-spawn", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "harness", "tmux", "sessions"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "src/PureClaw/CLI/Commands.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-frontend-harness-restart-reconnect-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "Restart reconnect for frontend harness sessions works because discoverHarnesses (boot) re-keys the shared harness map by tmux window name, which equals harnessKey = canonical<>\"-\"<>show windowIdx, which is persisted as TmuxConfig._tc_window in the session's _sm_kind. handleSend recomputes the key via harnessKeyFromKind and finds the rediscovered handle.", "recommendation": "Keep the three in sync: the renameWindow target, the _env_harnesses map key, and the persisted _tc_window must all be the same harnessKey string.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "harness", "tmux", "restart"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "src/PureClaw/Agent/SlashCommands.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-handrolled-test-main-registration-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "The Haskell test suite uses a hand-rolled test/Main.hs (NOT hspec-discover). A new spec module is invisible unless registered in BOTH test/Main.hs (import qualified + a describe ... .spec line) AND the pureclaw.cabal test stanza other-modules.", "recommendation": "When adding a spec module, register it in test/Main.hs AND pureclaw.cabal other-modules, or it silently won't run.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["testing", "haskell", "cabal", "build"], "affectedFiles": ["test/Main.hs", "pureclaw.cabal"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-frontend-toolchain-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "PureClaw has a React/TypeScript frontend in frontend/ (Vite + Vitest + TS strict). Gates: `cd frontend && npm run build` (= tsc && vite build) and `npm test` (= vitest run); there is no eslint script. The built output frontend/dist is GIT-IGNORED and served by Frontend/Server.hs (_fsc_staticDir) \u2014 build it for serving but do NOT commit it. There is no Haskell-style coverage gate on the frontend.", "recommendation": "For frontend changes, gate on `npm run build` (tsc strict) + `npm test`; rebuild frontend/dist for the binary to serve current UI but never git-add it (it's ignored).", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 2)", "date": "2026-06-02"}], "tags": ["frontend", "build", "testing", "vite", "vitest"], "affectedFiles": ["frontend/package.json", "src/PureClaw/Frontend/Server.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-runchat-shared-entry-no-runmode-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "runChat (CLI/Commands.hs) is the SHARED entry for both CmdTui and CmdGateway and does NOT know the invocation mode (only _co_channel distinguishes a little). Threading a per-run capability/policy signal (e.g. the adoption ConsentChannel) into the FrontendEnv requires adding a parameter to runChat and setting it in runCLI's `case cmd of` dispatch. The FrontendEnv record has exactly 4 construction literals (Commands.hs + test/Frontend/{StreamHarness,ActivityProbeSpec,APISpec}.hs) \u2014 the -Wmissing-fields cascade for any new field.", "recommendation": "To make a decision depend on how the binary was launched, add the signal as a runChat parameter sourced from runCLI's Command dispatch \u2014 it is not otherwise available at the FrontendEnv construction site. Expect the 4-literal FrontendEnv -Wmissing-fields cascade.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 3 \u2014 adopt external tmux)", "date": "2026-06-03"}], "tags": ["cli", "frontend", "run-mode", "haskell"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/CLI/Commands.hs", "src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-03T05:18:43.067377+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-03T05:18:43.067377+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-transcript-disk-is-aeson-encode", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "A transcript.jsonl line IS exactly `Aeson.encode entry` \u2014 Handles/Transcript.hs `_th_record` appends `LBS.toStrict (Aeson.encode entry) <> \"\\n\"`. So re-encoding a decoded TranscriptEntry via Aeson.encode is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the on-disk line (modulo the trailing newline): aeson 2.2.3.0 has ordered-keymap=True so the `_te_metadata :: Map Text Value` key order is canonical/sorted, Maybe fields encode as null stably, and Aeson.encode always emits valid UTF-8.", "recommendation": "To serve a byte-faithful 'raw' transcript line, use `encodeEntryRaw = TE.decodeUtf8Lenient . LBS.toStrict . Aeson.encode` (in PureClaw.Transcript.Types) \u2014 no need to thread original disk bytes through readTranscriptFile, and it makes the REST-reload and live-WS paths agree for free.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "pureclaw-1xd (feat/verbatim-raw-json)", "date": "2026-06-08"}], "tags": ["transcript", "aeson", "serialization", "hpc"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Handles/Transcript.hs", "src/PureClaw/Transcript/Types.hs"], "affectedServices": ["Transcript"], "createdAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-transcriptentryinfo-shared-wire", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "TranscriptEntryInfo (defined in Frontend/API.hs, single hand-written ToJSON) is the ONE shared frontend wire projection of a TranscriptEntry, constructed at exactly two sites: toTranscriptEntryInfo (API.hs, REST GET /transcript) and toEntryInfo (Stream.hs, live WS 'entry' event). It deliberately renames/drops fields (9 _te_* -> projected keys). EntryEvent.entry on the frontend (types/stream.ts) reuses the TranscriptEntry TS type, so a new field added on the backend ToJSON + the TS interface propagates to both REST and live paths.", "recommendation": "When changing the entry wire shape, update BOTH constructors (-Werror forces it since the record is shared) and regenerate the shared golden fixture test/Frontend/fixtures/stream-events/entry.json (consumed by BOTH backend StreamGoldensSpec AND frontend stream.test.ts).", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "pureclaw-1xd (feat/verbatim-raw-json)", "date": "2026-06-08"}], "tags": ["frontend", "transcript", "wire-format", "websocket"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "src/PureClaw/Frontend/Stream.hs", "frontend/src/types.ts", "frontend/src/types/stream.ts"], "affectedServices": ["Frontend.API", "Frontend.Stream"], "createdAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-08T01:30:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
